Bug: a rename does not find a symbol that only pass 2 defines

The parse that finds the symbol at the cursor (pushReferences() in refactory.c)
runs once, from the project baseline, without any pass's options. So -DPASS2 is
not defined and only2 is not seen: "No symbol found at the cursor."
Green at 7daee9dc and 499b84af, where the push went through the bridge and so
through processFile()'s loop over the passes. Red from 101a522c, which moved the
push off the bridge (WSL, session d25255b8, 2026-11-17).

The fix is the shape we want for every parse of a CU: one loop over the passes,
each starting the CU from the baseline plus that pass's options, and then the
input (a -D is lexed through the same input, so the pass comes first).
The refresh (parseFileWithFullInit()) and the request's own parse
(processFile()) already loop; the direct refactoring parses do not.
